**Appendix D: Draft Pilot KPI Framework**

*18-Month Pilot Evaluation Framework for Repositioned Digital Coach Role*

January 2026

**Overview**

This framework proposes measurable KPIs for an 18-month pilot of the repositioned Digital Coach role within the Quality/TLA team. It includes governance arrangements, review milestones, and demonstrates the capability to deliver against these measures. I have provided this to demonstrate how the repositioning and refinement of the role can benefit the college and continue to be accountable.

**Proposed Key Performance Indicators**

| **KPI Area** | **Measure** | **Data Source** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Teaching Quality Indicators** | Improvement trends in learning walk findings related to digital TLA; T8 achievement rates across curriculum areas | Learning Walk data; TLA profiles; Quality Team records |
| **QIP Traction** | Number of QIPs with digital inclusion actions; completion rate of those actions | QIP monitoring reports; HoA reviews |
| **Staff Capability** | Pre/post coaching survey scores; number of staff coached; repeat engagement rates | Coaching records; staff surveys |
| **Staff Confidence** | Self-reported confidence in digital pedagogy (survey); unsolicited testimonial themes | Annual staff survey; qualitative feedback |
| **Student Experience** | Learner feedback on engagement, clarity, and accessibility in digitally-enhanced sessions | Learner Voice surveys; Apprenticeship surveys |
| **Retention Proxy** | Qualitative feedback on workload reduction; frustration levels; anecdotal improvement signals | Staff feedback; exit interview themes |
| **Value for Money** | Case studies demonstrating time savings, cost-effective alternatives, reduced duplication | Documented examples; testimonials |
| **Digital Champions** | Network growth; project completion rates; peer support activity | Programme records; Teams analytics |

**Governance and Review Schedule**

| **Milestone** | **Focus** |
| --- | --- |
| **3 Months** | Initial state review: Baseline data established; coaching relationships initiated; early feedback gathered |
| **9 Months** | Mid-point review: Progress against KPIs; emerging themes; course corrections if needed |
| **18 Months** | Final report: Comprehensive evaluation; recommendation on permanent positioning; evidence portfolio |

*Governance: Quality Team leadership with reporting to Deputy Principal (Quality). Reviews shared with HR for consultation record.*

**Capability to Deliver: Skills and Experience**

The following qualifications and experience demonstrate capability to deliver against the proposed KPIs:

**Relevant Qualifications**

| **Qualification** | **Relevance to KPIs** |
| --- | --- |
| **DfE Certificate: Advanced Mentoring Skills for Experienced Mentors (July 2025)** | 27.5 guided learning hours + 18 hours workplace mentoring. Directly supports coaching capability and staff development KPIs. |
| **CMI Level 5 Diploma in Operational Management (in progress)** | Includes Managing Change, Stakeholder Relationships, and Coaching & Mentoring units. Supports governance and stakeholder engagement. |
| **Professional Diploma in Digital Learning Design (Distinction, 2023)** | Adult learning pedagogy and instructional design. Underpins digital pedagogy expertise. |
| **Postgraduate Certificate in Educational Leadership (2013)** | Excelled in Change Management. Supports organisational change navigation. |
| **PGCE (2006)** | Foundation teaching qualification with 19 years subsequent practice. |
| **Microsoft Certified Educator ****&**** Trainer** | Technical credibility for digital skills coaching. |
| **Mental Health First Aid Certificate (2022)** | Supports staff wellbeing dimension of retention proxy. |
| **Certified Member, Association for Learning Technology (CMALT)** | Professional recognition in learning technology field. |

**Relevant Experience**

| **Experience** | **Evidence of Capability** |
| --- | --- |
| **19 years teaching experience** | Credibility with teaching staff; understanding of classroom realities. |
| **12 years as subject leader** | Leadership experience; track record of improving outcomes. |
| **8 years in top 10% nationally (+0.7 residual)** | Evidence of consistent, measurable impact on learner outcomes. |
| **Coaching across 12 curriculum areas at Weston College** | Demonstrated ability to adapt approach across diverse contexts. |
| **Co-organised ****DigiWest**** conference** | Event management and CPD delivery at scale. |
| **Training delivery to 1,000+ staff (Futura Learning Trust)** | Experience scaling interventions across large organisations. |
| **Digital Champions programme coordination** | Community of practice leadership and network building. |
| **Quality Team collaboration on digital inclusion** | Direct experience of QIP integration and TLA support. |

**Conclusion**

This framework provides a structured approach to evaluating the repositioned role with clear, measurable outcomes. The combination of formal qualifications (including government-certified coaching capability) and extensive practical experience demonstrates capacity to deliver against these KPIs.

The 18-month pilot allows sufficient time to demonstrate impact while providing management with evidence-based data for permanent decisions.